\title{A level that, when reached, cancels every order on the instrument to free margin and then closes the whole position}
\description{
This is the Atlas's G12, a stop whose exit is not refused for margin. When the level is reached, UBI first cancels every order resting on the instrument at every broker, including orders placed outside UBI, because pending orders hold margin, and then closes the whole net position held in the instrument and the template's product with a limit two ticks past the other side's best price. It closes what is held when it fires, so the template's \code{quantity} is not used, and when nothing is held it completes without sending an order. Set \code{transaction_type} to the side that opened the position, so a long position is protected by asking for \code{buy}, which fires when the price falls to the level. \code{trigger_price} here is that level, not the order's own trigger. With \code{trigger_on}, the level is compared with the bid, the offer or the midpoint instead of the last trade, or must be reached on two ticks in a row (\code{double_last}) or for \code{hold_seconds} (\code{held}), so a single stray trade does not fire it. It answers HTTP 202 with an \code{outcome} of \code{armed} and sends nothing to a broker until it fires, so keep the \code{parent_id} from the answer. Only orders on the template's product are cancelled, since orders on another product belong to another position, and a change to the order's price or quantity while it waits is refused with HTTP 409.

The order template's attributes are described on \code{SyntheticOrder}.
}
